## ghostless

Local voice project. The corpus, transcripts, and gold edits stay on this machine unless you push the voice-data repository to a remote you chose.

| User intent | Skill |
| --- | --- |
| Draft something that sounds like me | `ghostless-draft` |
| Tighten or cut a draft I wrote | `ghostless-edit` |
| I finished a piece; learn from my edits | `ghostless-learn` |

- Read `voice-guide.md` in the project (`ghostless locate`). Run `ghostless build` if it is missing.
- Substantive rules live in `STYLE.md` (what a piece must prove) and `AUDIENCE.md` (who reads it); both are folded into `voice-guide.md` by `ghostless build`. Route a confirmed rule with `ghostless save --style/--audience`.
- After a draft, run `ghostless judge`.
- Leave a placeholder using the token named in `voice-guide.md` (default `[WRITER: your take]`) where an opinion, quote, statistic, or anecdote is needed. Do not invent those.
- For resumable edit sessions, start with `ghostless start draft.md` and finalize with `ghostless finish` (or run `ghostless learn` when both drafts exist), then `ghostless build`. `ghostless edit draft.md` opens the desktop editor when it is built.
- Review recurring edit hypotheses with `ghostless rules` and yes/no edit judgments with `ghostless checks`; confirm only what the writer decides.
